# Agent instructions

{{.Title}} is a [Tela](https://github.com/kuronosu/tela) app: a desktop UI in
pure Go (no cgo, no webview) with a React-like API and Tailwind classes.
Everything runs with `CGO_ENABLED=0`.

## Read first

Tela's guide for coding agents is `llms.txt`: the API, the `kit` components,
the agent loop and the common mistakes. Every Go block in it compiles.

- Online: https://telaui.dev/llms.txt
- The copy that matches the Tela version in `go.mod` (once the module is
  downloaded): `$(go list -m -f '{{"{{"}}.Dir{{"}}"}}' github.com/kuronosu/tela)/docs/llms.txt`

React names work as written (`UseState`, `UseEffect`, `OnClick`, `Key`) and
so do Tailwind v4 class names (`Class("flex gap-4 rounded-lg bg-primary")`).
`tela lint` reports an unknown class, role or key before you run anything.

## The loop

1. Write or change the UI.
2. Look at it without opening a window:
   - the `tela mcp` tools, if the client has them (`.mcp.json` starts the
     server): `snapshot` (aria YAML with refs), `screenshot` (PNG), `click`,
     `fill`, `press`, `inspect` (layout JSON), `lint`; or
   - `tela snapshot -o app.png .` and look at the PNG (`--size WxH`,
     `--scale N`, `--dark`, `--preview NAME`), `tela inspect .` for the aria
     tree and `tela inspect --layout .` for boxes and computed style.
3. Fix what is off and look again.

The screen is `var App` in `main.go` (or a `Preview()` function, or a
`Previews` variable with several named screens).

## Before you finish

```bash
tela lint ./...
CGO_ENABLED=0 go test ./...
```

Tests mount the app with `telatest` and run without a window: click with
`ByRole`, assert with `ExpectText`, add `Golden("name.png")` for pixels
(regenerate with `TELA_UPDATE=1` and look at the PNG).

## For a person

`tela dev` runs the app and reloads it on every save, keeping its state.
`CGO_ENABLED=0 go run .` runs it once. Install the `tela` command with
`CGO_ENABLED=0 go install github.com/kuronosu/tela/cmd/tela@latest`.
